IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccwa-jurisdiction`
IMPORT `ccwa-qa`

-- Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (ccwa-qa.l4): every exported question,
-- for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the three roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none:
-- the answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error.
-- Each question that takes the situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value under which it does not
-- arise (`it has not ended yet`, and for the three order questions also `the charge was dismissed` and `the child was
-- found guilty or convicted, and no order has been made yet`) and every later
-- input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. The situation is read through helpers that list every
-- value with no OTHERWISE, so the trap of graffiti finding 31 cannot hide a read of it.
--
-- For the child (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand from the text
-- (most taken from the baseline's own cases, ccwa-cases-jurisdiction.l4, with the life's event id), and once against
-- the baseline export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the parent, the victim
-- and the publisher, the values are worked by hand from the text. Jake was never charged (k022); facts beyond the
-- baseline's are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked charge` IS A `My charge`
ASSUME `an unasked bench` IS A `Who sits`
ASSUME `an unasked kind of custody` IS A `Kind of custody`
ASSUME `an unasked person` IS A `Person in the courtroom`
ASSUME `an unasked court` IS A `Where I am tried`
ASSUME `an unasked applicant` IS AN `Applicant`
ASSUME `an unasked recipient` IS A `Recipient`
ASSUME `an unasked ending` IS A `How the case has ended`
ASSUME `an unasked listener` IS A `Who I would tell`

`as the child` MEANS `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened`
`as the parent` MEANS `I am a parent or guardian of the child`
`as the victim` MEANS `I am the victim of the offence, or someone else affected by it`
`as the publisher` MEANS `I publish or broadcast reports, or would pass on what happened in the case`

